 Traders, I want to explain my trading style and get your input on it. Whenever I take a trade, I start with one lot. If I feel the trade is going in my favor, I gradually increase my position.

I also observe where the option price is finding support and wait for it to return to that level before adding more lots.

Additionally, I mark a few important downside levels where I believe the price could fall and use those levels to average my position. For example, today my last downside level for averaging was the 200 EMA, and I stopped adding more lots after that.

Do you think this is a good approach, or do you have any other preferred trading styles? Please share your thoughts.

